{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms","id":180962,"title":"EX3 Abyssal Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T10:34:42-07:00","id":180962,"title":"EX3 Abyssal Charms","content":"I may have watched an episode of Hannibal.<br /> <br /> <b>CRAFT</b><br /> <br /> <b>Magnificent Shrike's Display</b><br /> This Charm enhances a creation of the Abyssal's, making it fascinating and frightful in equal measure. It haunts the dreams of those who experience it, causing a madness of the deathknight's choosing.<br /> The target of this Charm must be subtly or overtly morbid, but needn't be a traditional Craft project -- written works, corpses, and dances are all appropriate vectors of madness.<br /> <br /> <b>SOCIALIZE</b><br /> <br /> <b>Songbirds and Corpses Decorum</b><br /> Once activated, this Charm renders those in the Abyssal's presence incapable of fear, offense, and disgust, as long as he seems courteous and maintains hospitality. Freakish contortionist-dancers elicit polite applause from those affected, while meals of live insects and human flesh seem to them as exotic curiosities.<br /> Piercing the deathknight's veil of etiquette requires an appropriate Major Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>SURVIVAL</b><br /> <br /> <b>Thorns Like Heavy Chains</b><br /> Watering the earth with her blood, the deathknight creates patch of thorns and pale flowers. The affected area becomes difficult terrain, and those who blunder through it are affected by a somnolent poison.<br /> <br /> <b>Thorns Like Long Knives</b><br /> An upgrade to Thorns Like Heavy Chains that allows the razor garden to fight like an immobile battle group. The Abyssal may use her Charms to enhance its attacks as though they were her own.<br /> <br /> <b>Thorns Like Red Poppies</b><br /> With this Charm, the Abyssal may sleep among her summoned briars without harm, shielded from environmental effects and dreaming of nothing. She heals faster when doing so, and can rid herself of certain Intimacies in her slumber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 07-28-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:51:27-07:00","id":181396,"title":"","content":"*hammering the Like button*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:10:20-07:00","id":181441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms#post180962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Songbirds and Corpses Decorum</b><br /> Once activated, this Charm renders those in the Abyssal's presence incapable of fear, offense, and disgust, as long as he seems courteous and maintains hospitality. Freakish contortionist-dancers elicit polite applause from those affected, while meals of live insects and human flesh seem to them as exotic curiosities.<br /> Piercing the deathknight's veil of etiquette requires an appropriate Major Intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How does one politely refuse a dish in circumstances such as these?&quot;<br /> &quot;One does not.&quot;<br /> *Gideon eats*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:50:19-07:00","id":181475,"title":"","content":"These are all fantastic. Thorns like Red Poppies and Songbirds and Corpses Decorum are my favourites.<br /> <br /> I have a bunch of ideas for Abyssal, Lunar, and DB charms that I am stubbornly sitting on until the core launches, at which point I'm going to make a thread for QC charms (since there will likely be demand for them at that time), and I do hope you will revisit these ideas then, and perhaps again when their book drops. I feel sad to see all these neat homebrew notions just being cast into the horizon like a paper boat on the ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T22:15:44-07:00","id":181665,"title":"","content":"<b>PERFORMANCE</b><br /> <br /> <b>Insidious Terror Narrative: </b>The Princess Magnificent with Lips of Coral and Robes of Black Feathers <i>learned</i> from her humiliation at Great Forks. She has studied the art of tale weaving and perverted it to her own ends: disinformation, manipulation and terror delivered through a pleasing, <i>desirable</i> package.<br /> <br /> After all, who doesn't love a good story?<br /> <br /> Abyssal with this charm emulates the Black Heron by laying siege to the minds of their opponents through rumor, prophecy or story. The death knight tells a story foretelling some doom happening under some omen or portent. Those listening resist a social attack as normal, except if they fail they do not suffer the effects immediately, the story buries itself in their mind like a latent disease... and gives them urge to retell the story.<br /> <br /> When they do, they use the same dice pool as the Abyssal who originally told the story. Even the most inept or introverted story teller will find themselves telling this wonderfully chilling campfire tale with the skill of a practiced master as friends crowd around to hear. Those who do also resist the story as a social attack, and, if they fail, become carriers as well.<br /> <br /> If the story carriers see signs that the events of the story are true, or coming true, they immediately suffer the effect of the dormant social attack. If no such sign occurs with (abyssal's essence) days the attack harmlessly dissipates.<br /> <br /> Ex: <i>The Death Knight Secret (full name too long to be written here) needs to rob a heavily guarded vault-wagon being transported in a guild caravan. Infiltrating the night's campfire under the guise of a humble caravan flea, she tells them the story &quot;Magistrate Bloody Fingers&quot;: a tale of particularly cruel and corrupt local judge who mutilated the hands of his victims in horrifying ways. He was eventually defeated by a band of heroic bandits, who threw the wicked judge's corpse into a bog on the night of a crimson moon. &quot;But beware!&quot; Secret says, &quot;On nights when the red moonlight shines on the bog, he walks again! Hungry for victims!&quot;<br /> <br /> The tale is a thrilling one, alleviating the numbing boredom of the road, it is soon retold to every member of the Caravan. On the third night, when the caravan is camping next to a swamp, a red moon rises and a cry rings out &quot;A hand! Someone nailed a hand to a tree!&quot; Guards rush to investigate, the priest begins reciting terrified prayers to the caravan god, and the caravan master hides in his wagon mumbling bargains of repentance to the Unconquered Sun if only his life will be spared.<br /> <br /> A chill falls on everyone in the caravan, all are too distressed to notice the shadow slipping into the vault wagon, disarming its locks and traps and then slipping out into the night...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 09-25-2014, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:51:23-07:00","id":211760,"title":"","content":"Suddenly, inspiration!<br /> Not as much as last time, though.<br /> <br /> <b>AWARENESS</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hideous Nightwalker Gaze</b><br /> For a scene, the Abyssal inverts all sight-based penalties from darkness and dreary weather, as well as from incense-smoke and other funereal sources. However, direct illumination turns the effect Obvious, as her eyes smolder, bleed, or otherwise reject the light.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Hunter's Samadhi</b><br /> With this Charm, Death's Lawgiver can percieve fear, feeling her victim's pounding hearts in her bones and tasting their dread in the sunset smoke coalescing around her. Difficulties are reduced for all rolls to notice and track the fearful, and the deathknight may discern if a fear is connected to an Intimacy with a standard (Perception + Awareness) roll.<br /> <br /> <b>MELEE</b><br /> <br /> <b>Jackal-Blade Ecstasy</b><br /> Touching a weapon, the deathknight enlightens it to the wonders of blood and death. As long as he commits motes to this Charm, the weapon deals more damage (lethal, if it didn't do so already). Further, anyone but the Abyssal who touches the weapon is considered to have a minor Principle of bloodlust while it remains in their possession, increasing to a major Principle if they actually wield it in battle.<br /> This Charm cannot enhance improvised weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>SOCIALIZE<br /> <br /> Wraith-Skin Regalia Assumption</b><br /> Summoning the spiritual detritus of his victims and former selves, the Exalted weaves them into baroque spectral finery around himself, or the body of another. In either case, the ghost-robe provides a circumstantial bonus to social rolls during court functions and other formal events, as well as <i>any</i> rolls to gain entry to the same. Additionally, the robe ensures that no infection spreads from the wearer, allowing even lepers to walk in Dynastic halls.<br /> As a final benefit, living wearers appear as ghosts to the dead, if only at first glance.<br /> <br /> <b>SURVIVAL</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dragons at Lord Death's Feet</b><br /> With a whisper, the Abyssal summons a beast to her side, calling down a vulture from the sky or a swarm of moths from the nearby woods. The animal (or swarm of lesser animals) must be a predator or scavenger, or bear some other symbolic connection to the dead.<br /> The omen of the deathknight's summons puts onlookers ill at ease, reducing their Resolve against fear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T19:10:15-07:00","id":259422,"title":"","content":"<b>BUREAUCRACY<br /> <br /> Coins from Open Graves</b><br /> Even away from her coffers, the deathknight is never wanting. She may turn any appropriately morbid materials (vials of blood, braids of corpse-hair, scraps of parchment bearing the names of the dead) into legal tender at will, sacrificing something in her distant treasury to use its value in the here and now.<br /> <br /> <b>RESISTANCE<br /> <br /> Scar-Tallied Sins</b><br /> Activated in response to a damaging attack, this Charm creates an unyielding intimacy of vengeance against the attacker and all they hold dear. Its intensity derives from the momentum behind the original attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Broken Bodies Satisfaction</b><br /> Letting go of one of his Scar-Tallied Sins, the Abyssal adds the momentum of the original attack to one of his own. This attack must be directed at the original attacker or one of their loved ones.<br /> Onlookers know that this is just retribution, and cannot move to prevent it.<br /> <br /> <b>Sycamore Sellsword Oath</b><br /> In return for some payment or favour \u2013 a name, a kiss, a bag of silver \u2013 the Abyssals swears to protect another. The steely cold of his promise marks his charge, as a warning to potential attackers, and he can sense when she is in immediate danger. The deathknight can send his shadow to Defend Other from afar.<br /> The Abyssal is wracked with pain when his charge comes to harm, doubly so if he is the cause of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T02:49:01-07:00","id":259635,"title":"","content":"I wish I could give these a like per Charm. (I might've written Coins from Open Graves to actually create temporary money rather than pull it from an already-extant cache, but.)<br /> <br /> If I may?<br /> <br /> <b>INTEGRITY</b><br /> <br /> <b>Darkness Swallows The Light</b><br /> Light, unlike darkness, is finite. There are some depths which it will never penetrate. This permanent Charm counters any Holy effect that directly affects the Abyssal, negating whatever additional effect it might ordinarily have against Creatures of Darkness. (This explicitly does <i>not</i> extend to any sort of detection magic.) The Abyssal also gains the incidental ability to ruin holy symbols of the Unconquered Sun with a touch (1A damage per round of sustained contact, for particularly large and/or durable icons).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I was also considering an expansion Charm that negated any effect with the Holy keyword entirely, but I guess I'd have to see the prevalence of Holy Charms in Ex3 to decide whether or not that'd be OP. Should be alright with a cost attached though, I'd think.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T03:43:50-07:00","id":259665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms?p=259635#post259635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I might've written Coins from Open Graves to actually create temporary money rather than pull it from an already-extant cache, but.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered it, but decided to go with the absurd, morbid ATM card model. This is a Charm that turns random bits of corpses into legal tender, forever.<br /> <br /> Note that it wouldn't actually cost anything, beyond the Resources value you assign to it. You just hand someone an eyeball, declare that it's money, and it <i>is</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T04:36:13-07:00","id":259688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms?p=259665#post259665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered it, but decided to go with the absurd, morbid ATM card model. This is a Charm that turns random bits of corpses into legal tender, forever.<br /> <br /> Note that it wouldn't actually cost anything, beyond the Resources value you assign to it. You just hand someone an eyeball, declare that it's money, and it <i>is</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can definitely see the appeal there. It's just that of all the characters I can readily imagine using a Charm like this, none of them would really have a distant treasury to draw on. (Well, I <i>do</i> have a very humorous mental image of the Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies rifling through his pockets for spare parts to pay off his bar tab, so there's one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T07:10:56-07:00","id":260587,"title":"","content":"Probably more Will Graham-y, but...<br /> <br /> <b>INVESTIGATION<br /> <br /> Assassin's Arrangement Appreciation</b><br /> <br /> This charm supplements an investigation of a murder scene, adding Essence automatic successes. Threshold successes gained while using this Charm allow for insight into the murderer: Minimal successes reveal only physical attributes, while higher successes detail the murderer's intentions, modus operandi, and connections to the victim not obvious from merely the physical evidence (for example, that the murderer loved the victim, even if this love had never been expressed to the victim).<br /> <br /> <b>Empathetic Adoption Epexegesis</b><br /> <br /> As an upgrade to the preceding Charm, the Abyssal may choose to assume one of the murderer's intimacies, and may add a number of successes to her investigation attempt equal to the strength of the new intimacy. Doing so also allows insight into the murderer's likely future actions, including potential victims or likely hiding places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T09:32:09-07:00","id":261295,"title":"","content":"As long as we're on media-inspired Charms, I know HIS EXCELLENCY DUKE OF ANKH-MORPORK COMMANDER OF THE WATCH BLACKBOARD MONITOR SAMUEL VIMES is totally a Solar, but:<br /> <br /> IMPLICIT ACCOMPLICE INTERROGATION<br /> <br /> The Abyssal is full familiar with that which witnesses all crimes and shameful sins, the cover of darkness. At the scene of a crime (or anything else that she wishes to know about), if she can put out all lights and sit in total darkness. Even a scene played out in partial light will be witnessed by the shadows, unless special precautions are taken to light every single spot. The Abyssal may ask up to (Investigation) questions of the darkness, but they should beware. Though the darkness with which the Abyssal communicates is not a sentient entity, many find that it seems to have some dark sense of humor, and delights in particularly depraved events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":1797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","user":"Ellis","date":".  Words, they sound the same, they're all the same, right :P 09-20-2014, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T10:21:13-07:00","id":263904,"title":"","content":"Something that popped into my head while listening to post-rock<br /> <br /> <b>PRESENCE<br /> <br /> Paint the Heart in Mourning</b><br /> <br /> This Charm targets any Intimacy related to someone that has died or something that has been destroyed. The Abyssal infects the Intimacy with profound melancholy, making it a rocky place where hope can find no purchase. Any attempts that appeal to the Intimacy fail, as the targeted person can only consider what has been lost.<br /> <br /> A repurchase of this Charm allows the Abyssal to infect not just the specific Intimacy, but any emotions/feelings attached to it. Those who have lost lovers will consider all future attempts at romance pointless, while the merchant prince who saw a treasured enterprise destroyed will be unable to muster any enthusiasm for a new economic endeavor.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Mirror: The Heart Is Not a Cold Dead Place</b><br /> <br /> As its Abyssal counterpart, this Charm targets any Intimacy related to someone dead or something destroyed. Instead of causing a permanent change, the Charm allows appeals to the Intimacy as if there had never been any destruction and they were still at their original strength. A repurchase allows the Solar to target the Intimacy as if she <i>was</i> the Intimacy, appealing to the widower with the strength of his lost wife and addressing the failed revolutionary with the force of his past conviction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T11:45:43-07:00","id":264008,"title":"","content":"Mirror Charms are deader than the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T11:48:32-07:00","id":264009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms?p=264008#post264008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirror Charms are deader than the Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wish this was true, but Holden has said that there will be at least a few charms that are effectively mirrors. I hope this simply means that both types will get a 'I ride good' charm, but he said despite an intention to remove as many of them as possible, there will indeed be at least a few charms that will functionally be mirrors. I hope this means that the Mirror keyword is dead as a doornail, but when I voiced my displeasure about Mirror charms, it was pointed out to me that they will exist in 3rd, along with a direct quote from Holden.<br /> <br /> Without seeing 3rd, it makes it hard to say exactly what they will be like, but something will continue to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:24:06-07:00","id":264124,"title":"","content":"I think Mirror in the sense of &quot;This Solar charm is at peak efficiency, so skin it Abyssal since they share the same power&quot; is still a thing.<br /> <br /> Mirror in the sense of &quot;There is no text here, please consult your other book&quot; is going to be less a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T12:06:29-07:00","id":264730,"title":"","content":"My sense is that the structure of the Abyssal and Infernal charmsets will involve a lot of charms that are similar (or even identical) to Solar ones at the roots of their trees, but which then branch out into much more bizarre directions from there. At least, that was how the spoiled Abyssal charms looked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:32:10-07:00","id":264920,"title":"","content":"I don't know if the Infernal Charmset will,* but that's a common trend from what's been said of Abyssals.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: Zakkeg</b><br /> From what I gather, it seems like a lot of [Abyssals'] foundational charmset will be functionally equivalent to what Solars get; it doesn't start really diverging until you go a few Charms up the tree.<br /> <br /> <b>A: John M\u00f8rke</b><br /> Some of their Charm trees will start off crazy different. My hope is to provide a lot of Charms that feel like mirrors without being mirrors.<br /> There will be some exact copies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Hungry Tiger Technique. Abyssals will have an identical mechanic. Some Charms just don't get any better.<br /> 2) It is stylistically accurate to depict the Abyssals as having deep connections to the Solars. EX3 Abyssals are radically different than they have been in previous editions. Having some identical Charms to Solars is a benefit, rather than a subtraction, because it emphasizes the fact that they were / are Solars, while also making them something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>* It would certainly make sense, I just think it's too early to say. There can be different ways to build a Charmset, even if trying to be evocative of another.<br /> <br /> Off-topic Infernal design speculation, ho! <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">From comments, EX3 Infernals seem meant to evoke the decadent sorcerer-king Solars of the First Age. For an alternative setup to Abyssals, I could see some Infernal roots looking like Charms that Solars get higher up in their trees, and then going off to odder places. These versions might be weaker, more constrained, less flexible or the like (or might not), but would evoke the sort of casual power and heights that Infernals get to fling around.<br /> <br /> Given what we've been told about Solar Charmtrees being generally designed in a sort of helix shape, it might also emphasize that simply having &quot;more advanced&quot; Charms doesn't mean as much on its own; in the Solar set, some such later Charms depend on being used with Charms earlier in the set to get the most out of them. Giving Infernals identical mechanics to those higher Solar Charms (albeit with lower prereqs) might work fine, and also subtly point to the idea of decadence (they're removed from more human fundamentals).<br /> <br /> Then again, the Infernals preview also showed mock-ups for a group of effects, of which the first (don't remember if it was prereq-free) amounted to &quot;become the Silent Wind.&quot; I doubt they'll just straight-up diverge, but we'll see.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Dropped spoilers around the on-topic quotes. 09-25-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:46:08-07:00","id":265149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms?p=264124#post264124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mirror in the sense of &quot;This Solar charm is at peak efficiency, so skin it Abyssal since they share the same power&quot; is still a thing.<br /> <br /> Mirror in the sense of &quot;There is no text here, please consult your other book&quot; is going to be less a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my impression as well.<br /> <br /> I believe the referenced example was Hungry Tiger Technique. In past editions it was hard to find mechanically better effects (more bang-for-your-buck as it were) than Hungry Tiger. Even at much higher Essence. If that paradigm continues, it makes sense for both Solars and Abyssals to have it the same. For Solars it's Melee puissance in striking with glorious might; for Abyssals it's Melee puissance at ensuring you only need one stroke to kill seven men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T23:08:26-07:00","id":265234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/180962-ex3-abyssal-charms?p=264730#post264730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My sense is that the structure of the Abyssal and Infernal charmsets will involve a lot of charms that are similar (or even identical) to Solar ones at the roots of their trees, but which then branch out into much more bizarre directions from there. At least, that was how the spoiled Abyssal charms looked.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with exploratory design on Abyssals is that there are a handful of &quot;lynchpins&quot; scattered along the Essence 1-5 scale, where there are effects that are just so solidly efficient and functional that mirroring the effect is the most elegant way to do it. Then you have all sorts of wild, horrific things growing off those like branches. <br /> <br /> (note that this is not reflective of developer vision or future mechanics, just me messin' around with writing Charms)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:31:27-07:00","id":265843,"title":"","content":"So long as its better than 2nd Ed. There were entire Abilities that only had mirror charms. Athletics, I'm looking at you in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:58:16-07:00","id":265870,"title":"","content":"<b>LARCENY<br /> <br /> Borrowed Years Masque</b><br /> <br /> Meditating on the timelessness of death, the Abyssal draws an advance on her limitless existence. While motes are committed to this Charm, the Abyssal may apply additional years to her natural appearance, and can become up to 50 years older than they normally are, allowing her to appear as an older mortal. This Charm automatically upgrades with each dot of Essence gained, allowing the Exalt to raise her age an additional 50 years per dot. After 100 applied years the Exalt may choose to appear as a walking corpse (gaining the Hideous tag(?)), and after 150 applied years the Exalt may appear as a living skeleton. This Charm does not affect physical attributes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}